            <ArticleTitle>[Studies on the internal pressure of bone tumors and tumorous conditions. I. Pain and internal hypertension of bone lesions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Internal pressure of bone tumors and tumorous conditions were measured in twenty patients. High pressure were frequently found in the patients with painful bone lesions while low pressures were common in the patients with no pain. High internal pressure may be a causative factor of aching bone pain at rest. It is suggested that venous obstruction without high internal pressure is not a causative factor of bone pain in simple bone cyst.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
